      "problem": "Which number corresponds to the midpoint of the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ if $A$ and $B$ are points on a number line that correspond to $-7$ and $1$, respectively?",
      "worked_solution": "The point $A$ corresponds to the number ${x}_{1}=-7$ while $B$ corresponds to ${x}_{2}=1.$ \n\nTo find the number ${x}_{m}$ corresponding to the midpoint $M$, we use the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7+1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{2} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14171842/assets/285fe00ff97923881624d984ed263955ce57d0f342832bbe367448d618cd4d1f.png)",
